  "method_summary": "D2Q9 lattice-Boltzmann with BGK collision, tau = 0.5 + 3*nu with nu = uin*square_size/re (contract formula; float64 throughout). Deterministic, exactly symmetric initial field: rho=1, u=(uin,0) on fluid nodes, u=0 inside the solid; f initialized at equilibrium (no random perturbation, no pre-settling). BCs: inlet x=0 fixed-velocity equilibrium (rho=1, u=(uin,0)); outlet x=nx-1 fixed-density equilibrium (rho=1) with velocity extrapolated from the penultimate column (standard pressure outlet, chosen after a zero-gradient outlet caused unbounded mass accumulation; with this outlet the global mean density stays within ~2e-3 of 1 over the full window); top/bottom specular-reflection free-slip walls (modeling assumption emulating an unbounded lateral domain). Obstacle: exact solid mask [cx-half, cx-half+size) x [cy-half, cy-half+size), half=size//2, treated with link-wise half-way bounce-back on all fluid->solid links. Force: momentum exchange per step from post-collision populations, contribution 2*f_i*(x)*c_i per boundary link; cd = Fx/(0.5*uin^2*size), cl = Fy/(0.5*uin^2*size). Time window: exactly n_steps updates, steps 1..n_steps, first warmup_steps steps excluded, (cd,cl) recorded only at steps with (step-warmup_steps)%sample_every==0. cd_mean = arithmetic mean of sampled cd; cl_rms = sqrt(mean(cl^2)) over the same samples. converged: mean cd of last 20% of sampled window vs first 80%: relative drift < 5% or absolute change < 1e-3. centerline 'u' = ux at y = square_center_y (final state, step n_steps); transverse 'u' = |u| magnitude and 'v' = uy at x_probe = min(nx-1, cx+2*size) (final state). cd_mean_avg = unweighted mean of per-case cd_mean. Initial field is exactly symmetric; no artificial asymmetry was injected, so near-zero cl indicates a symmetry-locked or symmetric-stable wake in this deterministic configuration.",
